WEBVTT

00:15.680 --> 00:17.330
Oh? Someone picked up.

00:17.870 --> 00:19.790
Wait, no one's there.

00:20.230 --> 00:22.710
This ain't what I heard.

00:22.710 --> 00:24.670
Al? It's you, right, Al?

00:24.670 --> 00:28.170
Seriously? Never thought
things would go this route.

00:28.770 --> 00:30.960
Right! Happy coincidence, lass!

00:30.960 --> 00:32.980
Yeah! What a really big coincidence!

00:32.980 --> 00:33.680
Right!

00:34.320 --> 00:36.890
Al, I need you to pass
a message to Subaru.

00:37.290 --> 00:38.390
S-Sure!

00:38.390 --> 00:40.310
I'll tell him you're safe and so—

00:40.310 --> 00:44.480
An Archbishop named Regulus
is occupying the tower in District 3.

00:44.480 --> 00:49.000
Also, the Archbishop of Lust
is in District 1's tower.

00:49.000 --> 00:49.990
O-Okay...

00:50.590 --> 00:53.410
I wish I could've investigated
the other towers,

00:53.410 --> 00:55.950
but I don't know where Sirius is.

00:56.490 --> 00:58.660
There was that broadcast, too.

00:58.660 --> 01:02.000
Tell him to protect Beatrice for me, okay?

01:02.000 --> 01:04.000
Oh, and...

01:04.000 --> 01:05.210
Wait up.

01:05.210 --> 01:08.340
I know you're a tough
and hyper-positive lass.

01:08.860 --> 01:10.800
But there's gotta be something else, yeah?

01:11.910 --> 01:14.760
This was all I could think of.
Did I miss something?

01:14.760 --> 01:15.850
That's not it!

01:16.350 --> 01:18.350
You're a damsel in distress right now!

01:18.350 --> 01:20.560
You don't need to force yourself
to do all this!

01:20.560 --> 01:23.600
You can ask our bro
Subaru Natsuki for help—

01:23.600 --> 01:25.820
I'm sorry for making you worry, Al.

01:26.230 --> 01:27.820
No, thank you for worrying.

01:28.330 --> 01:29.530
But I'm okay.

01:30.000 --> 01:31.320
You're okay...?

01:31.690 --> 01:34.610
I'm not trying to act tough.

01:34.610 --> 01:38.080
It might be strange of me to say this,

01:38.080 --> 01:41.330
but I've never doubted
that Subaru would come to save me.

01:42.000 --> 01:45.790
That's why I want to do everything I can

01:45.790 --> 01:48.980
to make it easier for Subaru
when he eventually comes.

01:50.470 --> 01:51.830
Please, Al.

01:51.830 --> 01:56.350
I'll apologize to Priscilla later
for ordering you around like this.

01:57.430 --> 02:00.730
Alright, I got it.

02:00.730 --> 02:03.810
I'll tell them what you told me.

02:03.810 --> 02:07.610
The rest is up to your Prince Charming.

02:07.610 --> 02:11.440
Subaru's the one who'll save me,
not a prince, though...

02:11.440 --> 02:12.700
Ah, right!

02:12.700 --> 02:14.160
My bad!

02:14.160 --> 02:16.890
But seriously,
don't pull any stunts, alright?

02:16.890 --> 02:18.530
This ain't a joke.

02:19.240 --> 02:20.160
Okay, I understand.

02:20.160 --> 02:22.190
You be careful too, okay?

02:25.780 --> 02:26.750
Thank goodness.

02:27.310 --> 02:30.210
Now my message will reach
Subaru and the others.

02:31.850 --> 02:36.590
Huh? Why am I so sure of myself?

04:09.050 --> 04:12.320
Do you know how to use this, Anastasia?

04:12.320 --> 04:14.280
Yeah, it's not hard to figure out.

04:14.890 --> 04:15.650
Alright.

04:15.650 --> 04:17.530
Looks like you're working hard, bro.

04:20.250 --> 04:21.200
Al!

04:21.200 --> 04:23.580
Well, someone's back early.

04:23.580 --> 04:26.910
Hey, it's not like I came back
just 'cause I felt like it!

04:26.910 --> 04:28.830
I've got a message for you, bro.

04:29.280 --> 04:31.040
A message? From who?

04:31.040 --> 04:33.710
Seems there's a lovely bride
waiting for her Prince Charming

04:33.710 --> 04:36.010
to whisk her away before her wedding.

04:36.010 --> 04:37.790
Wish I was you, bro.

04:38.590 --> 04:40.130
From Emilia?!

04:40.930 --> 04:43.600
And that's pretty much it.

04:44.030 --> 04:46.350
Oh, and she said to take care of Beatrice.

04:46.350 --> 04:49.850
Last part included,
that was some really important info.

04:50.290 --> 04:52.290
Extremely helpful, actually.

04:52.290 --> 04:53.190
Chief!

04:58.030 --> 05:00.280
- Garfie—
- Chief!

05:00.280 --> 05:01.850
You're okay!

05:01.850 --> 05:03.120
You sure popped out of nowh—

05:03.120 --> 05:05.160
That's my line!

05:05.160 --> 05:07.120
I thought ya were... I...

05:07.120 --> 05:08.540
I...!

05:08.960 --> 05:10.080
Hey now.

05:10.080 --> 05:12.170
Are you crying?

05:12.170 --> 05:14.040
I ain't cryin'!

05:14.040 --> 05:14.840
It's just...

05:15.370 --> 05:19.800
You, my bro Otto, Lady Emilia,
Beatrice... everyone's...

05:20.230 --> 05:22.220
Sorry to worry you.

05:22.220 --> 05:24.510
As you can see, I'm okay.

05:24.510 --> 05:26.970
Part of me kinda turned darker, though...

05:26.970 --> 05:28.770
Huh? Darker?

05:28.770 --> 05:31.100
Let's worry about that later.

05:31.100 --> 05:34.730
So? Do you believe all this, Natsuki?

05:35.750 --> 05:36.740
I do.

05:37.270 --> 05:40.950
The last bit about Beatrice
sounded just like her.

05:44.030 --> 05:48.570
She's doing everything she can
even in this mess.

05:49.620 --> 05:52.330
I want to believe in her.

05:52.760 --> 05:57.460
It'd be nice if she didn't overdo it
and try anything reckless, though.

05:57.460 --> 05:59.420
Can't deny that.

05:59.880 --> 06:03.750
That lass is way too energetic
for someone stuck in enemy territory.

06:08.810 --> 06:10.280
I'm surprised.

06:12.560 --> 06:14.650
I never thought you'd come back.

06:15.150 --> 06:17.610
You even left a convincing double.

06:17.610 --> 06:21.190
Huh? Double? I'm not sure
what you're talking about...

06:21.190 --> 06:23.780
I was tired,
so I was resting here the entire time—

06:23.780 --> 06:24.990
Ack, so cold!

06:24.990 --> 06:26.570
I mean, it's not cold at all!

06:29.790 --> 06:32.830
Why didn't you run away
while you could?

06:32.830 --> 06:35.210
I said I was resting here the entire...

06:39.190 --> 06:42.670
Did you... want me to run away?

06:44.710 --> 06:49.510
Why? If I ran, you and the other wives
would get in trouble.

06:50.390 --> 06:53.100
In the end,
it didn't amount to anything...

06:53.810 --> 06:57.650
I wanted to muster even a bit
of courage in my final moments,

06:57.650 --> 06:58.980
but it was all meaningless...

06:59.860 --> 07:00.820
#184...

07:02.410 --> 07:03.400
So?

07:03.810 --> 07:07.870
Why're we gathering here and what are we
gonna use this huge meteor for?

07:08.520 --> 07:11.830
This is the HQ
of the city reclamation team.

07:12.370 --> 07:16.370
And this meteor
is a city-wide broadcasting device,

07:16.370 --> 07:18.790
our ticket out of this mess.

07:18.790 --> 07:21.130
Ya got a plan, Chief?

07:21.560 --> 07:23.460
Something like that.

07:23.960 --> 07:25.420
As you all know,

07:25.420 --> 07:28.050
Wrath's Authority
has the entire city on edge,

07:28.050 --> 07:30.660
and the people are about to blow.

07:32.270 --> 07:34.140
Ya got that right, Chief...

07:34.140 --> 07:38.480
I was goin' around the city
lookin' for you, and...

07:38.860 --> 07:41.940
With the Witch Cult's broadcast
on top of the mess this city's in,

07:42.360 --> 07:44.040
it's only natural everyone's anxious,

07:44.500 --> 07:47.330
and it'll only get worse
with people crammed together.

07:49.260 --> 07:51.620
That's what makes
Wrath's power so insidious.

07:52.080 --> 07:54.790
It isolates people,
eats away at their hearts,

07:54.790 --> 07:56.660
and even threatens their lives.

07:56.660 --> 07:58.500
It is absolutely unforgivable.

07:59.000 --> 08:02.880
I reckon I already have a good idea
of what you're plannin' to do.

08:03.290 --> 08:06.840
Well, I did come all the way here
to see if the meteor was okay.

08:06.840 --> 08:10.320
What're ya plannin' to do, Chief?

08:12.250 --> 08:17.560
Sirius' Authority is amplifying
the anxiety of everyone in the city.

08:18.000 --> 08:21.400
And Lust's nasty broadcast
was what lit the fuse.

08:21.400 --> 08:22.520
Meaning...

08:22.930 --> 08:28.530
We reignite the people's hope the same way
the cultists fanned their unease.

08:28.870 --> 08:29.910
Right.

08:29.910 --> 08:34.910
We spread that hope
and fill the city with it.

08:36.440 --> 08:38.210
That's it!

08:38.210 --> 08:42.750
That'll get them back on their feet!

08:42.750 --> 08:44.090
Let's do it!

08:44.090 --> 08:46.050
There ain't time to waste! We gotta—

08:46.050 --> 08:47.300
Wait up.

08:47.300 --> 08:49.470
It's not as easy as it sounds.

08:49.470 --> 08:50.590
Why not?!

08:51.050 --> 08:54.140
What will the Witch Cult do
when they hear the broadcast?

08:54.660 --> 08:57.100
They might not close
the watergates this time.

08:58.100 --> 09:00.060
I'm worried about that too,

09:00.060 --> 09:02.770
but there's something off
about that theory.

09:02.770 --> 09:04.440
It's the watergate they opened.

09:05.610 --> 09:08.990
I see. That was District 1's gate.

09:08.990 --> 09:11.360
If Lady Emilia's information
is accurate...

09:11.990 --> 09:16.080
Then Lust can't be
at the control tower at that time.

09:16.440 --> 09:18.040
The timing's way too off.

09:18.040 --> 09:23.460
The flooding even helped us escape,
then the gate immediately closed after.

09:24.680 --> 09:28.340
It's true the Witch Cult's actions
are inconsistent at best,

09:28.340 --> 09:30.410
but there has to be
some logic behind them.

09:31.470 --> 09:35.930
They even left the meteor here unharmed.

09:35.930 --> 09:39.230
They should've had
plenty of time to break it.

09:39.230 --> 09:43.400
Are you sayin' us usin' this meteor
is part of their calculations?

09:43.800 --> 09:45.190
Why would they even—

09:45.190 --> 09:47.150
They don't have a reason for anything.

09:48.400 --> 09:49.030
Tch.

09:50.110 --> 09:53.780
They don't give a damn
about anything we do.

09:54.180 --> 09:58.660
They've never lost once,
and they don't think they ever will.

09:59.160 --> 10:02.920
A dragon doesn't care what the ants
crawling around its feet are planning.

10:04.290 --> 10:05.340
Natsuki.

10:06.380 --> 10:08.840
Let's go with your broadcast plan.

10:09.630 --> 10:11.090
Anastasia...

10:11.630 --> 10:14.260
So, who'll do it?

10:14.260 --> 10:16.010
"Who"...?

10:16.010 --> 10:19.390
Isn't this your time to shine, Anastasia?

10:19.390 --> 10:22.270
You're a royal candidate,
and you're famous around here.

10:22.270 --> 10:25.190
If you tell them
we're still fighting, they'll—

10:25.190 --> 10:28.480
You're expectin' too much of me.

10:29.450 --> 10:36.280
If fame was all it took, then sure,
I'd be more than happy to speak up.

10:36.780 --> 10:41.750
But my name alone doesn't have the
sway to rid their fear of the Witch Cult.

10:42.220 --> 10:46.290
Sure, it's better than some nobody,
but that's about it.

10:46.780 --> 10:50.130
It pains me to say it, since I'm basically
admittin' I'm not up to the task.

10:50.430 --> 10:51.800
Still...!

10:51.800 --> 10:53.590
You get it, don't you, Natsuki?

10:53.980 --> 11:00.010
They need hope, the kind that blows away
all the fear grippin' their hearts.

11:01.390 --> 11:04.150
If it's just pullin' wool
over people's eyes, sure,

11:04.150 --> 11:05.350
I can do it.

11:05.880 --> 11:09.270
But that's not what you're after,
right, Natsuki?

11:09.900 --> 11:14.320
You're the one who stubbornly
refused to cut our losses.

11:14.320 --> 11:15.640
Well...

11:16.170 --> 11:18.030
Th-Then what about Ms. Crusch?!

11:18.420 --> 11:20.700
Her words carried weight
back at the castle,

11:20.700 --> 11:23.050
and before the White Whale fight too!

11:24.200 --> 11:25.580
Right you are.

11:25.580 --> 11:27.500
But with the state she's in,

11:27.500 --> 11:31.300
we can't exactly drag her here
and make her stand in front of the meteor.

11:34.670 --> 11:36.970
Th-Then what about you, Julius?!

11:36.970 --> 11:38.750
You're more than qualified to...

11:38.750 --> 11:39.800
I'm sorry.

11:40.510 --> 11:42.680
I cannot meet your expectations.

11:45.000 --> 11:47.140
I'm proud to call Julius my knight,

11:47.540 --> 11:51.610
but how well do his feats
stack up against the Witch Cult?

11:52.270 --> 11:54.900
If we're just talkin'
about fame and eloquence,

11:54.900 --> 11:57.070
I'd have a better chance.

11:57.070 --> 11:58.360
Then...

11:58.360 --> 12:01.620
That leaves us
with Mr. Wilhelm and Ricardo.

12:01.620 --> 12:04.040
No, we can still call
Priscilla and Liliana—

12:04.040 --> 12:05.290
So, uh...

12:05.790 --> 12:08.500
Is there any reason
ya can't do it, Chief?

12:09.080 --> 12:09.880
Hah?

12:11.920 --> 12:13.210
You're our only chance.

12:13.650 --> 12:15.050
You're the Chief, after all!

12:15.590 --> 12:16.880
Who else could it be?

12:17.300 --> 12:23.100
You're the only guy
who's ever taken down an Archbishop!

12:23.100 --> 12:26.020
And right now, that means more...

12:26.020 --> 12:28.270
that means more than anythin'
in this whole city!

12:28.890 --> 12:30.350
Garfiel...

12:30.710 --> 12:32.940
With all these cultists
crawlin' around the city,

12:32.940 --> 12:35.610
there ain't no one better for the job!

12:35.610 --> 12:40.780
It's either the Sword Saint Reinhard
or Subaru Natsuki, no one else!

12:41.300 --> 12:43.990
It has to be you, Chief!

12:48.080 --> 12:50.040
He's right.

12:50.040 --> 12:53.290
If someone here's gotta do it,
it's gotta be you.

12:54.000 --> 12:56.010
Anastasia, not you too...

12:56.010 --> 12:58.020
Even you of all people?

12:59.630 --> 13:01.470
Do you remember, Subaru?

13:02.180 --> 13:06.540
Your outburst in front of
all those knights back at the castle,

13:07.020 --> 13:11.060
and how I defeated you
on the training grounds?

13:11.560 --> 13:16.110
It's one of my three biggest regrets
and humiliations of my life.

13:16.110 --> 13:18.940
I couldn't forget it even if I wanted to.

13:19.450 --> 13:21.780
I remember it well, too.

13:22.270 --> 13:24.280
Your baseless proclamation,

13:24.280 --> 13:26.540
the disgraceful way
you mocked the knights...

13:26.540 --> 13:29.250
...and how you joined
the White Whale fight...

13:29.780 --> 13:32.710
...and ultimately defeated Sloth afterward.

13:34.670 --> 13:36.960
If there is anyone in this city

13:36.960 --> 13:39.970
whose voice could rid the fear
gripping the people's hearts,

13:40.450 --> 13:43.390
I believe that person
is none other than you.

13:43.910 --> 13:48.720
Garfiel is only one of the many
who would answer your call,

13:49.220 --> 13:51.100
and I would be there as well.

14:00.530 --> 14:02.650
How can you overestimate me that bad...?

14:02.650 --> 14:04.990
If you're not sure, then don't do it, bro.

14:05.450 --> 14:08.910
Is this guy really that big of a deal?

14:09.660 --> 14:11.080
Shut your damn mouth!

14:11.080 --> 14:13.210
Don't ya talk that way about the Chief!

14:13.210 --> 14:16.460
If only he could bear
the weight of the world,

14:16.460 --> 14:17.750
that'd be incredible.

14:17.750 --> 14:22.380
But you can't expect an average,
everyday guy to carry all that.

14:22.920 --> 14:25.590
I can't, and our bro here can't either.

14:26.610 --> 14:29.560
Yet why does he have to shoulder all that?

14:31.100 --> 14:32.520
Give the poor guy a break.

14:34.770 --> 14:35.900
Hey, bro.

14:36.410 --> 14:40.820
That girl's what you care about
most right now, yeah?

14:41.290 --> 14:43.900
I'm gonna do what I can for the Princess.

14:43.900 --> 14:47.700
Everything else can wait.

14:48.360 --> 14:49.540
Al...

14:49.930 --> 14:51.580
You should too, bro.

14:51.580 --> 14:55.500
Focus on the lass... on saving Emilia.

14:55.500 --> 14:59.840
Just think of those damn cultists
as a passing storm.

14:59.840 --> 15:02.460
Getting involved will only
bring you more trouble.

15:15.980 --> 15:19.110
If a kid runs out into an intersection
when the light's red,

15:19.110 --> 15:22.650
you'd pull them back to the sidewalk
without a second thought, right?

15:23.740 --> 15:25.860
It's kinda like that.

15:27.780 --> 15:29.830
If you're gonna do it, bro,

15:30.230 --> 15:33.790
you're gonna carry the full weight
of that heroic delusion.

15:34.250 --> 15:36.250
Heroic delusion...?

15:36.600 --> 15:39.590
You can't afford to lose.
You have to win.

15:40.040 --> 15:44.840
You'll carry hope, shoulder expectations,
and lead everyone to the future.

15:45.270 --> 15:48.050
Make that choice,
and you'll have to follow through.

15:48.450 --> 15:51.310
Can't afford to lose?
That's always how it's been.

15:51.310 --> 15:53.180
The stakes are gonna be higher!

15:53.180 --> 15:56.770
Your loss ain't gonna be
just your loss anymore.

16:04.240 --> 16:06.320
My name is Emilia!

16:11.660 --> 16:13.620
You're in full oni mode, after all.

16:19.620 --> 16:21.170
Thank you, Subaru...

16:21.740 --> 16:24.880
Thank you for saving me!

16:31.850 --> 16:36.520
Subaru! Subaru! Subaru! Subaru!

16:38.440 --> 16:42.150
Eh, just the same as usual, then.

16:43.770 --> 16:46.170
Don't make that face, Garfiel.

16:47.780 --> 16:51.780
Chief... Chief! Chief!

16:51.780 --> 16:53.910
Chief, you really are the Chief!

16:53.910 --> 16:55.880
You're not making any sense.

16:56.540 --> 16:58.500
I'll do it, Anastasia.

16:59.120 --> 17:02.270
If my voice can do something
about this mess, then I'll do it.

17:03.000 --> 17:07.260
You sure? If you turn
into our symbol of hope...

17:07.260 --> 17:09.630
I'm just gonna do what I always do.

17:09.630 --> 17:12.340
A hero, eh? Nice ring to it.

17:12.340 --> 17:15.680
It's pretty embarrassing
to call myself that, though.

17:16.180 --> 17:18.230
But if it's just playing
the role of the hero,

17:18.230 --> 17:20.230
I made that decision a year ago.

17:20.730 --> 17:23.570
If I run, I won't be able to face
the girl who's looking at me,

17:23.570 --> 17:26.020
and I'll never catch up to the girl
I'm looking at.

17:26.020 --> 17:28.400
That so? Go get 'em, then!

17:28.900 --> 17:31.610
Boys always try to look cool, after all!

17:35.410 --> 17:37.240
Don't laugh if I flub, okay?

17:37.240 --> 17:38.260
No sighs either.

17:38.260 --> 17:39.710
If possible, don't listen at all!

17:40.240 --> 17:43.750
I will not laugh, nor will I sigh.

17:43.750 --> 17:46.880
I will listen closely until the end.

17:48.800 --> 17:51.220
Thanks for worrying about me, Al.

17:51.930 --> 17:53.830
You helped me make up my mind.

18:15.780 --> 18:16.910
It would've been better

18:17.330 --> 18:21.790
if I was consumed by Lord Husband's anger
because you didn't return.

18:22.290 --> 18:25.750
Now, all that's left for me
is this never-ending status quo...

18:25.750 --> 18:29.550
In that case, why not stand
and try again with me?

18:29.550 --> 18:32.010
I haven't given up yet.

18:34.260 --> 18:37.970
I can't... not anymore...

18:41.560 --> 18:46.020
You're free to decide
that you won't give up.

18:46.020 --> 18:49.110
But I'll never be tempted
to hope ever again.

18:49.610 --> 18:51.360
I'm sure the other wives are the same.

18:51.360 --> 18:52.320
No way...

18:52.760 --> 18:56.910
I was just an ordinary girl
living in a tiny village.

18:57.450 --> 18:59.620
To marry me,

18:59.620 --> 19:03.870
Lord Husband went after my father,
mother, siblings, neighbors,

19:03.870 --> 19:07.210
and even the other villagers
who only knew my face and name...

19:07.210 --> 19:09.380
...and killed every last one of them.

19:11.710 --> 19:14.470
All his wives suffered the same fate.

19:21.810 --> 19:25.440
Ah, ahem! Uh...

19:25.440 --> 19:28.610
Can everyone actually
hear me through this?

19:29.440 --> 19:30.570
Subaru!

19:31.360 --> 19:33.150
Mic test, mic test!

19:33.150 --> 19:35.320
One-two, one-two!

19:36.280 --> 19:38.910
Nice, looks like you guys can hear me.

19:39.530 --> 19:43.370
Oh yeah, first,
I'm sorry for startling you.

19:43.370 --> 19:47.290
I know a lot of you are worried
about hearing another nasty broadcast,

19:47.290 --> 19:48.420
but don't worry.

19:48.910 --> 19:52.630
The guy talking to you right now
isn't a cultist.

19:52.630 --> 19:54.510
- I just wanted to clear that up first.
- He's not a cultist...?

19:55.000 --> 19:57.300
Th-Then... are we saved...?

19:57.300 --> 19:59.720
Did they chase them away?

19:59.720 --> 20:04.090
Sorry to get your hopes up,
but we're not in the clear yet.

20:04.660 --> 20:06.480
We've taken back the city hall,

20:06.480 --> 20:09.120
but the control towers
are still in their hands.

20:09.860 --> 20:11.570
Their demands still stand,

20:11.570 --> 20:14.610
and the city's still in danger of flooding.

20:14.610 --> 20:16.400
I thought you needed to know that.

20:16.990 --> 20:18.250
I'm sorry.

20:20.520 --> 20:24.200
To everyone listening,
where are you right now?

20:24.200 --> 20:29.210
I'm sure some of you are in the shelters,
and some of you weren't so lucky.

20:29.840 --> 20:32.250
You guys must be so anxious right now.

20:32.250 --> 20:36.840
I'm sure some of you must be wondering
who the hell I think I am

20:36.840 --> 20:40.000
for getting your hopes up.

20:41.160 --> 20:44.560
I'm nobody, just your regular guy.

20:44.560 --> 20:47.890
I'm just a guy thrown into this mess
like the rest of you.

20:47.890 --> 20:51.730
My feet are shaking, and I'm about
to be crushed by the unfairness of it all.

20:52.150 --> 20:53.820
Just like you.

20:54.180 --> 20:59.650
To be honest, I think broadcasting this
is too much for someone like me.

20:59.650 --> 21:05.700
There's gotta be someone else
better for this job.

21:05.700 --> 21:07.120
I'm sure of it.

21:07.120 --> 21:10.710
But right now,
I'm the only guy you've got.

21:10.710 --> 21:16.680
The people who're way better than me
said it should be me.

21:17.170 --> 21:19.300
They said it'd be
more meaningful this way.

21:20.800 --> 21:23.350
My voice is shaking right now, isn't it?

21:23.350 --> 21:26.220
I'm not the kind of guy who'd stand
in front of a crowd.

21:26.220 --> 21:31.230
I don't know how to make a fancy speech
or have the charisma to lead you guys.

21:31.600 --> 21:34.310
I'm weak and pathetic.

21:34.310 --> 21:36.110
Even in an important moment like this,

21:36.110 --> 21:37.690
- I can't help but want to run away.
- Sis...

21:38.440 --> 21:41.200
I don't know what to do.

21:41.200 --> 21:43.570
I want to plug my ears,
curl up into a ball,

21:43.570 --> 21:49.290
and ignore everything while
someone else solves everything for me.

21:50.480 --> 21:51.620
No...

21:53.470 --> 21:56.000
Even so, I'm going to fight
since I can't run away.

21:56.520 --> 21:58.460
That's just the sort of guy I am.

22:02.320 --> 22:03.890
Let me ask you again.

22:04.470 --> 22:07.180
To everyone listening,
where are you right now?

22:07.710 --> 22:09.640
Did you flee to a shelter?

22:09.640 --> 22:11.690
Are you hiding in your house?

22:12.070 --> 22:14.000
Are you trembling all alone?

22:14.000 --> 22:15.870
Are you with someone right now?

22:16.440 --> 22:19.650
Is that person someone precious to you?

22:19.650 --> 22:23.860
Or maybe it's a stranger you've come
to know over the last few hours.

22:24.570 --> 22:27.660
I know it's not my place to say this,
and I know it's hard for you,

22:27.660 --> 22:30.370
but please, don't shut yourselves away.

22:31.340 --> 22:34.920
When you're alone, it's easy to get lost
in meaningless thoughts.

22:34.920 --> 22:37.590
I know. I've been there.

22:37.590 --> 22:40.260
So please, don't shut yourselves away.

22:40.260 --> 22:42.260
Stay with someone else.

22:42.260 --> 22:43.300
And...

22:45.130 --> 22:46.930
And if you can...

22:46.930 --> 22:49.510
Try to look at that person in the eye.

22:52.020 --> 22:54.190
Whose face are you looking at right now?

22:54.810 --> 22:55.900
Someone precious to you?

22:56.300 --> 22:59.650
Is it a stranger you've come to know
over the last few hours?

23:00.650 --> 23:02.900
I'm sure they look awful right now.

23:02.900 --> 23:05.570
Maybe they're crying, or in pain.

23:05.570 --> 23:07.720
I doubt anyone's smiling right now.

23:08.280 --> 23:10.200
Are you really okay with this?

23:10.740 --> 23:11.750
Of course not...

23:11.750 --> 23:14.830
I'm not. I refuse to accept this!

23:15.230 --> 23:17.130
I too have people I care about,

23:17.130 --> 23:19.000
and comrades dear to me!

23:19.000 --> 23:25.220
I won't let those who put sad or pained
looks on their faces get away with it!

23:25.560 --> 23:26.970
Don't mess with me.

23:27.390 --> 23:29.100
I'm not stupid!

23:29.100 --> 23:33.390
I know her real smile
is way cuter than that!

23:33.390 --> 23:34.850
I want to be able to say that!

23:35.390 --> 23:37.290
I can't let them beat me forever!

23:37.290 --> 23:39.620
I'd never be able to live it down
if I gave up now!

23:39.620 --> 23:41.730
I won't accept being
pushed around like this!

23:42.300 --> 23:44.780
They're the ones at fault.

23:44.780 --> 23:47.740
I'm not going to sit back
and let the bad guys win!

23:48.170 --> 23:52.160
I don't want to accept defeat
against scum like them!

23:52.160 --> 23:53.700
So I'll fight.

23:53.700 --> 23:58.540
I know I'm dumb and weak,
but I'm going to fight anyway!

23:58.540 --> 24:00.500
They're the ones in the wrong!

24:00.500 --> 24:05.010
They're wrong for making the people
I care about sad!

24:05.010 --> 24:06.340
So I'll fight!

24:06.340 --> 24:07.800
I'll keep fighting!

24:08.260 --> 24:10.280
And I want you guys to fight too!

24:11.390 --> 24:13.140
Don't misunderstand me, though.

24:13.140 --> 24:16.020
I'm not telling you to take up arms.

24:16.020 --> 24:18.270
What I want from you

24:18.270 --> 24:21.000
is to keep your head up!

24:21.690 --> 24:23.480
Head... up...?

24:23.820 --> 24:27.240
Nothing's gonna change
if you keep staring at your feet!

24:27.240 --> 24:30.700
So keep your head up!
Look at what's in front of you!

24:31.240 --> 24:34.660
If you look around,
you'll definitely meet someone's gaze!

24:35.120 --> 24:38.500
They might be scared like you

24:38.500 --> 24:42.210
but they're also someone
who doesn't want to lose.

24:42.650 --> 24:44.710
C'mon, let me believe in it!

24:44.710 --> 24:48.680
I'm weak and pathetic,
but I haven't given up yet.

24:49.300 --> 24:52.350
Let me believe that
I'm not the only weakling

24:52.350 --> 24:54.430
who doesn't know when to give up!

24:55.140 --> 24:57.890
Or is it really just me?

24:59.020 --> 25:00.350
Nope...

25:00.680 --> 25:03.310
No, of course not.

25:03.310 --> 25:05.900
Am I the only one who thinks
we can still do this?

25:05.900 --> 25:07.650
That we still have a fighting chance?

25:07.650 --> 25:08.700
Is it really just me?

25:09.090 --> 25:10.610
- No!
- No, you're not!

25:10.610 --> 25:11.660
Of course not!

25:12.090 --> 25:13.750
No, I'm okay.

25:14.310 --> 25:16.120
I can still keep going.

25:16.520 --> 25:17.870
It's not just me, right?

25:18.330 --> 25:19.370
It's not!

25:19.830 --> 25:21.340
Right. It's not just you.

25:21.340 --> 25:22.750
You're definitely not alone!

25:22.750 --> 25:24.630
I know it
from the bottom of my heart!

25:25.020 --> 25:27.010
You guys can still fight, right?!

25:27.010 --> 25:29.090
You're not letting weakness
consume you, right?!

25:29.090 --> 25:30.800
I won't lose! I don't want to lose!

25:30.800 --> 25:31.930
They're not beating us!

25:32.570 --> 25:35.390
I'm fine.
I can hear your voice, after all.

25:35.810 --> 25:37.480
Nothing can scare me now.

25:40.890 --> 25:43.190
If the person beside you
is special to you,

25:43.190 --> 25:45.440
hold their hand and believe!

25:45.810 --> 25:47.690
If the person beside you is a stranger,

25:47.690 --> 25:50.740
give them a nod and stand together!

25:50.740 --> 25:55.240
Keep on fighting so neither you
nor that person will break!

25:55.730 --> 26:00.080
As long as you guys don't give in,
I'll keep on fighting too!

26:00.500 --> 26:02.540
I'll fight...

26:02.540 --> 26:04.960
I'll fight and win!

26:05.420 --> 26:07.750
My name is Subaru Natsuki!

26:07.750 --> 26:11.720
The spiritmancer who defeated
the Witch Cult's Archbishop of Sloth!

26:12.220 --> 26:15.300
Leave these cultists to me and my allies!

26:15.300 --> 26:18.310
So please trust us and keep fighting too!

26:18.680 --> 26:23.520
Hold the hand of that special someone
and blast away that despair and weakness!

26:24.230 --> 26:29.940
Then leave the rest to me!

26:33.400 --> 26:34.990
That broadcast just now...

26:35.700 --> 26:37.330
That was my knight.

26:37.330 --> 26:39.370
He's always really trying his best.

26:40.500 --> 26:42.210
I won't run.

26:43.080 --> 26:45.540
I won't leave you girls behind.

26:47.670 --> 26:48.750
Why?

26:49.180 --> 26:55.220
You must've been so scared,
but you still tried to help me.

26:55.760 --> 26:59.640
I want you and the other girls
to find happiness too.

27:00.170 --> 27:05.060
Marriage is a ceremony to bring happiness
to two people who love each other.

27:05.060 --> 27:08.360
The bride has to be happy, too.

27:11.070 --> 27:15.530
I know people who loved each other
but couldn't get married.

27:16.490 --> 27:19.700
Even today, my heart still aches
when I think about them.

27:20.620 --> 27:22.950
A marriage should be happy.

27:22.950 --> 27:25.330
Nobody should have to endure
a relationship like yours.

27:25.730 --> 27:28.210
Y-Your thoughts are commendable,

27:28.210 --> 27:30.830
but if you're going to do something,
please do it alone.

27:30.830 --> 27:32.210
Alone...?

27:32.860 --> 27:34.670
No, that's not right.

27:35.200 --> 27:37.800
I was never alone.

27:38.680 --> 27:39.680
That was dangerous.

27:39.680 --> 27:41.390
I almost forgot that just now.

27:42.180 --> 27:43.730
What are you planning to do?

27:47.920 --> 27:49.610
We're going to hold the wedding.

27:54.820 --> 27:57.110
It's finally over...

27:57.110 --> 27:58.570
That was rough...

27:58.570 --> 27:59.750
Natsuki.

28:04.290 --> 28:07.040
I'm so sorry!
I'll do better next time!

28:07.040 --> 28:08.420
Why're you apologizin'?

28:08.420 --> 28:09.580
What a strange sort.

28:11.370 --> 28:13.380
That was a splendid speech.

28:13.380 --> 28:15.880
Chief, ya really are the Chief!

28:15.880 --> 28:18.010
Well, I'll be!

28:18.010 --> 28:19.470
With a tongue like yers,

28:19.470 --> 28:22.640
no wonder ya've tricked all those ladies,
kiddies, and land dragons!

28:22.640 --> 28:25.100
Natsuki's a natural instigator, after all.

28:25.450 --> 28:29.560
I never tricked anyone,
and "instigator" isn't a compliment!

28:36.240 --> 28:39.360
Do you think I cheered them up a little?

28:40.870 --> 28:43.450
All that's left is to get rid
of the source of all this.

28:43.450 --> 28:48.000
Yeah, and to do that, we're going
to have to retake all four towers.

28:48.000 --> 28:51.420
Then how about we play our trump card?

28:52.290 --> 28:53.610
Otto!

28:55.210 --> 28:58.230
My bro Otto! You're okay!

28:58.230 --> 28:59.430
It was a close call,

28:59.430 --> 29:01.510
but I managed, somehow.

29:02.190 --> 29:05.310
Anyway, I've brought him with me.

29:06.830 --> 29:08.270
Brought who?

29:17.360 --> 29:18.990
Apologies for the wait.

29:21.360 --> 29:23.950
Reinhard van Astrea...

29:25.950 --> 29:29.170
THE NEWEST HERO AND THE OLDEST HERO
...though late, has joined the fray.

29:29.170 --> 29:29.960
THE NEWEST HERO AND THE OLDEST HERO
